        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "033be310-e18a-4b72-88ee-3b51afbf2b5a"
        },
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail",
          "scroll": "page"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='font:400 18px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;padding:32px;color:#0f172a;background:#ffffff;height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto'><div style='font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>START WITH YOUR AI</div><h1 style='margin:16px 0 8px;font:600 40px/1.1 system-ui'>Start with your AI</h1><p>Talk with your AI about what you want to make. It will put it here.</p><ol><li><b>Start your AI.</b> Click the Twilite icon in the top bar. It copies what your AI needs to know. Paste it into a chat with your AI. It will tell you it understands, and ask what you want to make.</li><li><b>Talk it through.</b> Tell your AI about a project, a story, a plan, or an idea. Talk until there is something worth keeping. It may offer to put it in a graph, or you can ask for one.</li><li><b>Bring its reply back.</b> Click the paste icon in the toolbar, paste what your AI wrote, and choose Run. Then ask for more in the same chat and paste each reply the same way, or change a card yourself.</li><li><b>Look around.</b> Zoom out until each card shows only its title, then in until it shows everything. One graph, three sizes. Click a card to select it.</li><li><b>Save it.</b> Saving is part of the editor. With it, click the save icon in the top bar, then Save As: Save locally downloads the file, Save to GitHub keeps it in your repository.</li><li><b>Come back.</b> Another day, choose Open graph from the same menu. Your graph is as you left it.</li></ol><p>It worked when the stage fills with what you described.</p></div>"
        },
        "memo": "The Detail view: the page in full. The Method writes it from the masthead, the section and the routes, so edit those and not this.",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
