      ],
      "style": {
        "background": "#39291b",
        "color": "#fff1d2",
        "borderColor": "#daa65a",
        "borderWidth": 3,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# INDIANA JONES\n\n### The Scholar Who Refuses to Stay in the Library\n\n**Archetype:** Adventurer / Explorer / Reluctant Hero\n\n**Motivation:** Discovery, preservation and the pursuit of historical truth.\n\n**Greatest strength:** Resourcefulness under impossible pressure.\n\n**Greatest weakness:** Obsession, pride and a spectacular fear of snakes.\n\n**Internal conflict:** Scientific skepticism versus extraordinary experience.\n\n**Character arc:** Learning that the people beside him matter more than the treasures ahead.\n\n---\n\n*He isn't the strongest man in the room. He isn't the most dangerous. He's simply the man who keeps getting back up.*"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "cfef98fa-2f89-4b39-b69f-b2bbcfc3ba74"
        },
